MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Train Of Thought feels like a natural next choice after 10.000 Days because I want heavy music with intricate arrangements that reward close listening.",
    "City of Evil, Mezmerize, and The End of Heartache fit different parts of my listening: melodic riffs, shifting rhythms, and harsh vocals balanced with melody. Those qualities connect with my interest in In Flames, Soilwork, and heavier rock."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Shot to Hell and Load lean toward bluesy heavy rock or a hard rock sound, while I want more intensity and intricate playing today.",
    "Framing Armageddon's theatrical concept focus does not appeal to me right now; wanting elaborate musical arrangements does not mean I want an elaborate story."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in heavy music seems to have been treated as a broad preference, even though groove, melody, and musical complexity affect whether an album feels right today.",
    "Several albums fit my general taste, but that alone does not make me want to choose them together. WAKING THE FALLEN and Lost and Found interest me, yet I already have stronger choices for this visit."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest interest in 10.000 Days makes intricate, heavy arrangements especially appealing now, which is why Train Of Thought is my first choice.",
    "The balance of melody and aggression matters: I am drawn to heavy riffs with melodic movement or contrasting vocals, rather than heaviness by itself."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in heavy music, but only some captured the melody, intensity, and intricate arrangements I want most right now."
}
